OL,3,ATrain attack driver had '10 seconds' to
OL,4,Achange line
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe driver of a high-speed train where
OL,7,Fa mass stabbing took place said he had
OL,8,F"probably about 10 seconds" to decide
OL,9,Fto switch to the slow line before
OL,10,Fmaking an unscheduled stop.
OL,12,FAndrew Johnson was driving the
OL,13,FLondon-bound LNER service on 1 November
OL,14,Flast year when the train stopped at
OL,15,FHuntingdon in Cambridgeshire amid a
OL,16,Fmass attack by Anthony Williams.
OL,18,FGiving evidence, Johnson told jurors at
OL,19,FCambridge Crown Court he heard someone
OL,20,Fon the intercom "screaming 'there's a
OL,21,Fknifeman stabbing people'".
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
